  <page_number>652</page_number>
  <running_head>CONFUT. PSEUD-</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>Sed Scientia &amp; ars recensitus differunt.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>Ergo.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">Majorem qui neget, ostendere tenetur,</l>
    <l n="4">alia esse majora discriminis realis do-</l>
    <l n="5">cumenta : ex abundanti tamen ita pro-</l>
    <l n="6">bari potest :</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Quacunque accidentia eidem communi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>subjecto inexistentia differunt omni-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>bus proprijs qua habent, illa</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>differunt realiter.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Sed quacunque accidentia eidem com-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>muni subjecto inexistentia differunt</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>recensitis, differunt omnibus proprijs</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>qua habent. Ergo differunt realiter.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Et porro : Scientia &amp; ars sunt</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>talia accidentia. Ergo si recensitis diffe-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>runt, realiter differunt.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18" para="true">Major planissima est: Minor autem</l>
    <l n="19">probatur: quia accidentia eidem</l>
    <l n="20">subjecto inexistentia non habent plura,</l>
    <l n="21">quam suam essentiam, causas, subjectum,</l>
    <l n="22">&amp; consequentia. Sequitur igitur</l>
    <l n="23">conclusio.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Minor argumenti principalis per</l>
    <l n="25">singulas partes deducenda est: Et quidem</l>
    <l n="26">1. <i>quod definitione scientia &amp; ars diff-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>erant</i>, clare notavit Arist. l. 6. Ethic. c.</l>
    <l n="28">3. &amp; 4. ubi diversas illarum definitiones</l>
    <l n="29">ponit. 2. <i>quod principijs differant</i>, patet:</l>
    <l n="30">Quippe Philosophus l. 6. Eth. c.4. l.1.</l>
    <l n="31">Phys.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword and signature absent. Text of the first line "Sed Scientia" is italic. Some letters in the scan are damaged at the page edge (lower left), but the text is legible.</notes>
